<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72d1eec290e42776ee25302c60c2456e1cdc5b1bb0259d7e70cf82331b6d12df</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone unnoticed for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18b11963eb9e26381d6b032cfacd7c9b305e55365abf5b4d4f66950bba0d8f0f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-unnoticed-for-months/a-79281803--5e7710f3265e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-unnoticed-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:303d5ac1c9b5175f77c6513bc683d1b8d52479ea33f6e2edcf53311c353e354f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:061098c4944d9d39934c12e7c9be9899e29e5c763748ab5969a850b4b714234a</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adfbb3509a139b92ea4702b3163be172b6be25afe9b5f883e9121c1d5846cd9b</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e9f6956d10410519add8a17ff9026776ad9fa5ae693196f2a9da7ab49c4a74b</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia faces hard choices as Houthis gain in Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ba454b634b3c573d3d9eb99b6be407df733f04962744a868cf759845ebef5f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826--836e117689a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia faces growing security and economic problems as it seeks to balance deterrence and diplomacy during its escalating conflict with the Iran-backed Houthis in neighboring Yemen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e3db92e5d170c5310cc55eff8289c61fc3ec17d59b49f5525900a958e23a2a0</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fb5bddfa1bb3e90fd026a5fd15399a5b95d6b2842bf68531fafd1ebd88f651f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on amid war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c41da6141bc1e47f299b7eac309999e7e4e90e776a20cc3fae5b6e1ac85f2346</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123--af9edc52c450.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9af242a9efebbb0a022e8c51d7b916f12e3ae0e5096b5f02009f9a7528e5aa04</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e4331f64a2d48cd870bb118f35ea9df850096acc54dc9953759edf12004f3dd</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a531a321f72d166a54c67270a49c2462969604dbefe5286f05eccb5e8062ef6</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
